// Rules (same as the workbook's Read Me):
//  - Hours: one reading per truck per week (start / end meter). Check = End < Start · Over max (100 hrs / week) ·
//    Below prior week (start under the previous week's end) · Unknown serial · Excluded (Exclude = Y). Only OK rows
//    feed the asset's hour meter, reading date and average hours / week (last 8 OK weeks).
//  - Service: Last PM = latest Preventive Maintenance service date; Next PM due = Last PM + PM interval (90 days);
//    PM status = Overdue · Due in 14 Days · Current · Not Scheduled. Open items = Status Open; days open from the
//    service date. Spend YTD = invoice amounts this year.
//  - Operators: Expired (expires before today) · Expiring in 60 Days · Check Dates (expiry on or before the card date)
//    · Missing Expiry · Current (the workbook's "Active"). Prerequisites: classroom, practical, evaluation, date certified, card issued, trainer.
//  - Leases: Lease End = start + term months; payments made = whole months from start to today (+1 paid in advance),
//    capped at the term; remaining obligation = remaining payments + buyout until the lease ends.
import { store } from '@atl/store.js';
import { excelDate, norm, num, isISO, todayISO, addDays } from '@atl/util.js';
import { bldgOfMheSite, seesAll, canSee } from '@atl/sites.js';

//  - Equipment management (V58): each unit has a Status (In Service · Out of Service · Retired) with a dated history,
//    maintenance work orders (Reported → Under Review → Scheduled → In Progress → Completed), inspections with
//    deficiencies and corrective actions, and documents / photos. A work order is mirrored into the Service Log
//    (id WO-<work order>), so Last PM / Next PM, spend and the service reports include it. Records are never deleted:
//    units are retired, work orders cancelled.
//  - Lockout / tagout (V59): each lockout (LOTO-0001 …) is the Lockout Tagout Log (Piper LOTO policy, Attachment C;
//    OSHA 1910.147): unit, reason, energy sources and how they are isolated, stored energy, verification, and every
